  "rationale": "Pareto target: latency (epsilon 2000ms). The `summary` field is the largest text contributor per section (bigger than citations which round 1 already trimmed). Current rule permits 1-3 sentences with a soft preference for 1-2; tightening to strict 1-2 (default 1, second allowed only for a named substantive reason) plus banning transitional padding removes ~1 sentence from ~30-40% of sections. Estimated savings: ~1000-1800 chars (~5-8% of output_chars_mean=21325) \u2192 ~2500-4500ms latency drop, clears 2000ms epsilon. Quality floor holds because (a) the second-sentence carve-outs cover exactly the content that completeness-oriented summary_quality judges reward (thresholds, cross-refs, exceptions), (b) banned patterns are pure padding, not information. Expected summary_quality delta: -0.01 to +0.01 (well within 0.03 regression band; could even improve if judge rewards concision). Different file/field than round 1's citations.md edit, so not a repeat. No clash: identity (`faithful short summary`), hierarchy, citations, exclusions, output_schema do not constrain sentence count.",
